# Screens for the InitechDOS 3.30 User's Guide (1024-3300-11), beads initech-ipu5.7 / ipu5.6.
# name|serial marker[#count]|disk
# The keystrokes of screen NAME are screens/NAME.keys, one line read with
# printf %b (\n = Enter, \\ = backslash); it is the ONLY keyboard source
# (test-pubs SCREEN-KEYS). Only noautoexec keys start with the two Enters
# that answer startup date/time.  The marker is text of the LAST
# command's output; #count is how many times it has appeared on the serial
# mirror (typed keys echo there too) when the screen is complete.  disk is
# the practice diskette the screen boots with (pubs/screens/disk/MANIFEST):
# empty = the practice diskette as shipped, whose AUTOEXEC.BAT sets PATH;
# noautoexec = the same diskette without AUTOEXEC.BAT, the only case in
# which InitechDOS asks for the date and time at startup (initech-qskz).
# Regenerate with "make pubs-screens"; "make test-pubs-screens" re-captures
# every screen and diffs it against the book.
startup|A:\>|noautoexec
errors|Required parameter missing|
dir|bytes free|
type|Copies of the cover sheet|
copy|bytes free|
del|File not found|
paths|bytes free|
ren|bytes free|
wild|A:\PHONE.TXT|
cdsub|bytes free|
tree|None#2|
vol|Volume in drive A is INITECH|
label|Volume in drive A is WORKDISK|
chkdsk|bytes free|
backup|bytes free|
